## Goal

Build and qualify a distinct CUDA-JS WSL2 x64 profile. WSL2 uses Linux user space with a Windows-host Driver bridge; it is neither native Linux evidence nor native Windows evidence.

Follow the [F7 WSL2 handoff](https://github.com/iteathen/CUDA-JS/blob/main/conformance/f7/README.md), the [F8 package handoff](https://github.com/iteathen/CUDA-JS/blob/main/conformance/f8/README.md), and the [hardware qualification program](https://github.com/iteathen/CUDA-JS/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-08-11-hardware-qualification-program.md).

## Required work

- classify the host as `wsl2-x64` and reject WSL1;
- define canonical Driver-bridge and toolkit-provider discovery without arbitrary path expansion;
- preserve the accepted generated ABI, actor ownership, public facade, and permission boundaries;
- run independent Driver/context, memory, PTX execution, NVRTC/nvJitLink/cache, failure, repeated-lifecycle, installed-package, and cleanup capsules;
- record Windows host, WSL kernel, Node, Driver bridge, providers, GPU, and compute capability in sanitized form;
- add a runner-ready profile only after every native capsule exists;
- run the complete profile from one clean exact commit and submit the standardized evidence bundle.

## Acceptance

Node and independent native oracles agree, permissions fail closed without authority, output checksum is exact, aggregate close is terminal, and no raw pointer/provider path/native object crosses the public facade. Promotion applies only to the exact WSL2 profile.

Do not use this result to close the native Linux x64 issue or claim ARM64 support.

## Goal

Create and qualify the native Linux ARM64 SBSA CUDA-JS profile as an independent ABI and runtime target. x86-64 schema or execution evidence cannot qualify ARM64.

Use the [F7 ARM64 handoff](https://github.com/iteathen/CUDA-JS/blob/main/conformance/f7/README.md), [hardware support list](https://github.com/iteathen/CUDA-JS/blob/main/docs/HARDWARE_SUPPORT.md), and [qualification program](https://github.com/iteathen/CUDA-JS/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-08-11-hardware-qualification-program.md).

## Required work

- official Node v26.7.0 ARM64 identity and native glibc/SBSA host record;
- hash-pinned official CUDA 13.3 ARM64 headers and providers;
- independent native C size, alignment, offset, function-pointer, and calling-convention oracle;
- ARM64 Runtime IR and generated products rather than reused x86-64 layout claims;
- canonical Driver, NVRTC, builtins, and nvJitLink discovery with exact versions/digests;
- complete F2 through F8 Driver/context/memory/execution/compiler/permission/package/cleanup chain;
- standardized sanitized qualification bundle from one clean exact commit;
- registry and support-list promotion limited to the exact passing profile.

## Guardrails

SBSA and Jetson are separate deployment/provider profiles. Cross-compilation, portable controls, and package import do not prove native execution. Do not regenerate expected ABI values merely to match a failing host.

