- alter the private Research Wiki;
- alter IDE/project configuration;
- run commands whose purpose is cache cleanup or maintenance.

Use read-only inspection commands only. Prefer `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` for Git inspection where applicable. For current remote truth, use GitHub read APIs and/or `git ls-remote` rather than mutating local refs with `git fetch`.

Dry-run/listing modes are allowed only when documented to make no changes, e.g. `git worktree prune --dry-run --verbose` or `git clean -ndX`; record the exact command and verify it was dry-run only.

Do not execute any proposed cleanup command.

## Claim-specific authority

| Claim | Authority |
|---|---|
| Current authoritative repository state | current remote `main` + GitHub durable state |
| Local checkout/worktree truth | direct read-only inspection of the Linux filesystem and Git metadata |
| Current work contract | this Issue |
