## Historical/durable replacement rule

An old specification, review, export, manuscript copy or migration artifact may be a `REMOVE-CANDIDATE` only when the Review proves a durable authoritative replacement exists and that the local artifact has no remaining evidential role.

Evidence may include:

- exact hash identity with a committed durable artifact;
- an authoritative GitHub Issue/PR/file that explicitly supersedes it;
- an accepted release/source registration;
- a verified archive already containing the exact artifact.

Filename similarity, newer timestamps or “looks obsolete” are insufficient.

Historical manuscripts remain reference artifacts under `NO_ACTIVE_MASTER`; do not assume they are disposable merely because they are not active masters.

